options.explanation:
Since $1\text{ liter}=1000\text{ centimeters}^3$, we know that both $\dfrac{1\text{ liter}}{1000\text{ centimeters}^3}$ and $\dfrac{1000\text{ centimeters}^3}{1\text{ liter}}$ equal $1$.

So we can multiply by either of those fractions to help us convert units, since multiplying by $1$ doesn't change value. In this problem, we multiply by $\blueD{\dfrac{1\text{ liter}}{1000\text{ centimeters}^3}}$ since the quantity we want to convert is in $\text{cubic centimeters}$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}100\,\dfrac{\cancel{\text{centimeters}^3}}{\text{kilometer}}\cdot \blueD{\dfrac{1\text{ liter}}{1000\,\,\cancel{\text{centimeters}^3}}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{100}{1000}\,\dfrac{\text{liters}}{\text{kilometer}}
\end{align}$
